          "fig-16-y-axis-extent",
          "fig-16-axes-perpendicular"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "fig-16-source-circle-and-extrema",
        "description": "Visible ink: one solid unfilled closed circle centered at the axes crossing and the existing upper-right x^2+y^2=100 equation. Source has no independent point dots at O or the four circle-axis extrema. Radius 10 and exact extrema are equation-bound regularization. Hidden origin/extrema are construction additions only, not source-visible point objects, and need no source pointRelationships group. All unchanged radius/displacement assertions remain mapped and executable.",
        "objects": [
          "fig-16-circle",
          "fig-16-circle-equation"
        ],
        "assertions": [
          "fig-16-one-circle",
