          "fig-16-bottom-on-circle"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "fig-16-source-line-terminals-intersections",
        "description": "Visible ink: one solid descending finite line with x+y=-2 text, two labelled intersections A(-8,6) upper-left and B(6,-8) lower-right. Source has no independent dots at its top/bottom frame cuts. Exact (-16,14) and (11,-13) hidden terminals are unchanged equation/frame-bound construction additions, not mapped source-visible points. A/B point emphasis and upright equation typography remain existing modern additions. A and B are the only mapped point objects; unchanged A-to-B displacement covers both wholly within this group. All old terminal/incidence/origin relationships remain executable without claiming those anchors are visible.",
        "objects": [
          "fig-16-source-line",
          "fig-16-line-equation",
          "fig-16-A",
          "fig-16-B"
        ],
